# LeakSanitizer suppressions for `just asan` (docs/audit/2026-09-23-sanitizer-report.md).
# Only leaks that are not ours and that we cannot free belong here. Each entry
# matches any frame of the allocation stack. Keep them narrow enough that a
# leaked mlt++ wrapper of ours still reports (report finding S1): such a
# wrapper is allocated by `new` inside libmlt++/our code, never under
# mlt_factory_producer, so it is not hidden by the entries below.

# MLT's module repository, allocated once by Mlt::Factory::init (fixed ~14 KB).
leak:Mlt::Factory::init
leak:mlt_factory_init

# MLT's loader leaks the normaliser filters it attaches to every producer it
# creates, including the "blank" producer mlt_playlist creates internally
# (report finding S3; upstream). Per-producer and not freeable from our side.
leak:mlt_factory_producer

# SDL audio (via MLT's sdl2_audio consumer, sdl2-compat over SDL3): hint
# cache and mutexes SDL never frees because the audio subsystem is never
# shut down.
leak:libSDL3.so
leak:libSDL2

# App session only (report's "not ours" table): font caches, and AppWindow,
# which main.cpp leaks on purpose for the process lifetime.
leak:libfontconfig.so
leak:libpango
leak:ustudio::app::onActivate

# FFmpeg worker-thread buffers (decode/encode threads spawned via MLT's avformat
# module). `just asan` LD_PRELOADs these libraries so they stay mapped after
# Factory::close() unloads the module and their frames can be symbolized.
leak:libavcodec.so
leak:libavutil.so
leak:libavformat.so
leak:libswscale.so
leak:libswresample.so
leak:libx264.so

# p11-kit's library constructor (newlocale), pulled in by libavformat -> GnuTLS
# when the libraries above are preloaded.
leak:_p11_kit_init

# GDK's display GL setup, reached from gtk_init_check() in the GTK-widget
# tests (dropin-shell): the EGL driver's own state, allocated once per
# process when the display opens and never freed by GTK.
leak:gdk_display_init_egl

# movit's glsl.manager (ADR-019): GlslManager holds a reference of its own
# through its mlt++ base, so after every caller's reference and the global
# one are gone it is still never freed (MLT's filter_glsl_manager.cpp).
# One per manager created: the probe, and each time GPU is switched on.
# `just asan` preloads the module so these frames symbolize.
leak:filter_glsl_manager_init

# Our own EGL display (platform::GlContext, ADR-019): initialised once per
# process and never terminated by design, so the driver's screen, configs
# and option tables stay, as with GDK's display above; the first context on
# a screen also adds per-screen state below it. A GlContext we leak still
# reports: our wrapper is allocated outside these calls.
leak:eglInitialize
leak:eglCreateContext

# MLT's movit.convert (filter_movit_convert.cpp, MLT 7.40): convert_image()
# makes an MltInput for every input of every frame and parks it in the
# frame's properties with no destructor; only a frame that builds a new chain
# hands it on, so with a reused chain each one leaks (about 1.2 KB an input a
# frame: ~10 MB a minute of GPU playback at 30 fps with five inputs). An
# upstream bug we can't free from outside (the type is private to the
# module). The Flatpak's MLT carries the fix
# (packaging/flatpak/patches/mlt-movit-convert-input-leak.patch); this
# stays for distro MLT builds.
leak:create_input

# The effects drop-in's tests (drop-ins/effects/tests), MLT-internal and
# one-off; `just asan` preloads the modules so these frames symbolize.
# - A module's metadata callback (the frei0r module's parameter info): 1.6 MB
#   lost once when every filter's metadata is read. The editor never reads
#   metadata in its own process, only the render tool's registry child.
leak:mlt_repository_metadata
# - The avformat module's swscale normaliser: one image block lost once per
#   process when a frame read smaller than the profile passes an alpha
#   filter between mask_start and mask_apply (a keyframed effect mix); it
#   didn't grow over more frames or four more graph builds.
leak:filter_scale
# - The frei0r module's own allocations for a filter it creates: a few bytes
#   each for some plugins, freed by nothing. A leaked mlt++ wrapper of ours
#   still reports (it's allocated outside the module).
leak:libmltfrei0r.so

# MLT's avfilter filter (libmltavformat, filter_avfilter.c:431/711, MLT 7.40):
# init_image_filtergraph() closes its temporary properties only on failure;
# the success path returns first, so each filter graph set-up (the first
# frame, a format or size change) leaks them. Upstream; the effects drop-in's
# avfilter.* effects (a LUT) reach it. Inlined into filter_get_image, which
# only MLT's own filters have on a stack: our wrappers are never under it.
leak:filter_get_image
